P0012 521..524 10:1 only a binding chain (`2048 -> hidden_size;`) may stand at the top level; wrap other statements in a function
P0003 617..623 14:5 a bare expression is not a statement; flow it (`-> target`) or make it the block tail
L0008 804..827 21:5 guard discriminant exceeds the maximum value (u64::MAX); value clamped
P0004 804..827 21:5 stray guard arrow outside a guard block; `-7-> x` reads as a guard arm. If you meant a negated value flowing to a target, add a space: `-7 -> x`
    fix 804..827 "-99999999999999999999 ->" — add a space inside the would-be guard arrow
P0005 948..957 27:9 guard arrows are written without interior spaces
    fix 948..957 "-true->" — remove the spaces inside the guard arrow
P0115 1078..1122 34:12 anonymous block stage (`-> { … }` with statements/tail) is out of Mapal-Core (HANDOFF §4); user-guide §8.3 full-language form. Planned for Core+1
P0006 1107..1116 36:9 statement mixed with guard arms in the same block; a guard block contains only arms. If you meant a guard arm, remove the space: `-7->`
P0007 1218..1219 42:11 comparison operators are non-associative; parenthesize (e.g. `(a < b) < c`)
P0008 1307..1309 47:12 only one `<-` binding per statement (W17); chained `<-` is not Mapal-Core
P0009 1408..1410 52:7 `<-` cannot appear inside an expression; `i<-1` lexes as `i <- 1`. For a comparison write `i < -1`
    fix 1408..1410 "< -" — did you mean `< -` (comparison with a negative)?
P0010 1495..1497 57:10 empty block `{}` in stage position — classified as a zero-branch fanout
P0001 1565..1566 61:11 expected `:` and a parameter type
P0002 1676..1677 66:12 unclosed `{`
